  "rationale": "With Elektron program changes on, the next-slot program change was sent when current_step == global_pattern_length - 1. At length 2 that fired at Play, naming the next slot before slot 1 sounded, and each later announcement coincided with its boundary; at length 1 no transition was ever announced. Arbitrated SEM-013 (final-step-short-lengths, Claude-only, unanimous): lengths of three or more keep the two-step lead; lengths 1 and 2 announce the next slot on the final step, after its notes, from an order-4 sprocket on the master's division, computing the next slot from the state the next pulse's song switch reads.",
  "oracle": "README Elektron Program Changes (1086): each song pattern change on Mosaic is mirrored by the Elektron devices so both stay in sync; a Digitakt queues a received program change to the end of its current pattern, so the change must precede the boundary.",
